From 7419279a624d3f0916722c8a0d983ed1fb53442f Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajhochy <ajhochy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 02:09:14 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 04/10] fix(desktop): align Open Design theme inputs
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Remove token-map.ts's internal light/dark color resolution — it silently
diverged from ThemeContext.getBaseColors for dark-first built-ins with no
darkColors (e.g. midnight), painting the raw dark seed instead of the
synthesized light palette. buildOpenDesignThemePayload now takes an explicit
resolvedColors snapshot the caller must supply (activeTheme.colors or
getBaseColors), eliminating the ambiguity instead of re-deriving a guess.

Also add a raw-authority precheck in origin.ts before new URL() parsing:
WHATWG URL normalizes shorthand/hex/integer IPv4 literals (127.1,
0x7f000001, 2130706433) into 127.0.0.1 during host parsing, which would
otherwise let those forms trade on the loopback allowlist. Only the exact
literal strings 127.0.0.1 and [::1] are now accepted as a host.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Sonnet 5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
