From 57596b72875d2ffc2005e53fc6cec9e75a846029 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: ajhochy <ajhochy@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 20 Aug 2026 13:33:45 -0700
Subject: [PATCH 09/10] fix(desktop): repair Open Design final-review findings
 (v4)
MIME-Version: 1.0
Content-Type: text/plain; charset=UTF-8
Content-Transfer-Encoding: 8bit

Repairs all seven independently reviewed S3 final-review findings with
strict vertical TDD, one behavior test per finding before its fix:

1. A bounded CSS-trivia scanner classifies direct rgb()/rgba()/color(srgb)
   constructors after skipping leading comments before the keyword and
   between color( and srgb, so `/**/rgb(calc(300) 0 0)` and
   `color(/**/srgb 300 0 0)` fail closed instead of bridging a
   CSSOM-clamped value; renderer-valid relative-RGB/color-mix/oklch with
   leading trivia and in-range commented constructors still resolve.
2. Style/observer ownership (bumped to v4) now treats every exact
   v1/v2/v3 owner as legacy, enumerates only real <style> elements,
   dedupes duplicate current owners, and requires a verified
   (Reflect.set + readback) neutralization or a genuine disconnect()
   before retiring any owner — aborting before installing an opposing
   observer if neither can be proven. A valid current owner is reused in
   place (no observer growth); an invalid one is retired and replaced,
   never double-observed. The callback self-disconnects when detached
   and no-ops when live ownership/desired-theme no longer matches.
3. `--glass-regular` is added to the versioned allowlist, derived from
   the resolved panel surface as `color-mix(in srgb, <panel> 66%,
   transparent)`, and scoped under `@media (prefers-reduced-transparency:
   no-preference)` so Open Design's own reduced-transparency fallback
   stays authoritative. Coverage is asserted from an independently
   sourced pinned-token list, not the bridge's own allowlist.
4. Semantic surfaces resolve before their paired foreground/border
   fields, which now composite alpha over the actual resolved
   destination (card, popover, primary, secondary, accent, midground,
   destructive, sidebarBackground, userBubble) instead of root
   background. Terminal colors flatten over the resolved terminal/root
   background instead of implicit black; only selection-background
   alpha is still intentionally preserved.
5. Radius and shadow offset/blur/spread each carry an explicit,
   documented magnitude budget enforced after CSSOM resolution, so
   `1e308px` geometry is rejected while normal values at the exact
   budget still pass.
6. `buildOpenDesignThemeInjectionScript` rejects any payload whose
   schemaVersion isn't the current constant, and
   `injectOpenDesignTheme` treats a resolved execution result as
   untrusted: only an exact plain `{ok:true, styleId}` object survives,
   rejecting wrong ids, extra keys, inherited/array values, and
   throwing accessors/proxies.
7. The URL gate rejects the complete Unicode `Cc` control category
   (C0, DEL, and all of C1 U+0080-U+009F) in raw candidate and expected
   input, closing the same-origin-path bypass for raw U+0080..U+009F
   while still accepting percent-encoded controls and normal SPA paths.

Verified: 256/256 focused open-design-theme tests, 5388/5388 full UI
tests, typecheck, changed-file + full lint clean, production build +
postbuild artifact assertion, and a real Electron 40.10.2 (Chrome
144.0.7559.236) probe against the actual bundled library (54/54 checks)
covering all seven findings plus prior-round regressions.

