+ * connected computed-style capture normalizes every length to `px` except
+ * percentages (see `host-snapshot.ts`), so any other unit reaching this
+ * validator is either a raw/structural snapshot that bypassed canonicalization
+ * or an attempt to smuggle a larger real magnitude (e.g. `10000in` is
+ * 960,000px) under a budget documented and enforced in pixels. Alternate
+ * units are therefore rejected outright rather than compared by raw
+ * magnitude across units.
+ */
+const CSS_LENGTH = new RegExp(`^(${CSS_NUMBER})(px)?$`, 'i')
 
